Package: rrcsurv
Type: Package
Title: Risk Set Regression Calibration for Survival Models with Error-Prone Time-Varying Exposure
Version: 0.0.0.9003
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yue", "Yang", email = "yueyang@g.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Donna", "Spiegelman", role = "aut"),
    person("Molin", "Wang", role = "aut"))
Description: Corrects for measurement error in a cumulative (time-varying) exposure in Cox proportional
    hazards and linear excess relative risk (ERR) survival models by risk set regression calibration
    (RRC). Supports additive and multiplicative measurement error models fitted in a main/internal or
    main/external validation study, confounder adjustment, and a sandwich variance that accounts for
    the estimated calibration parameters.
License: GPL (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/fyGuo/rrcsurv
BugReports: https://github.com/fyGuo/rrcsurv/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: stats, survival, utils
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
